{"version": 2, "width": 120, "height": 40, "timestamp": 1789369334, "title": "Pyvider provider-native linting proof", "env": {"TERM": "xterm-256color", "SHELL": "/bin/bash"}}
[0.5, "o", "\u001b[1;36m$ tofu version\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.56, "o", "OpenTofu v1.13.0-beta1\r\non darwin_arm64\r\n+ provider registry.opentofu.org/provide-io/pyvider v0.5.0\r\n"]
[0.562, "o", "\u001b[1;36m$ tofu validate\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[5.91, "o", "Success! The configuration is valid.\r\n"]
[9.641, "o", "PASS: provider linting default-off (0 provider lint diagnostics)\r\n"]
[9.641, "o", "\u001b[1;36m$ PYVIDER_LINT=provide-io/pyvider:all tofu validate -lint=all\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[12.608, "o", "\r\nWarning: Experimental linting enabled\r\n\r\nThe linting functionality is under active development and may change or break in future releases. You can provide\r\nfeedback by opening a new issue.\r\n"]
[12.609, "o", "\r\nWarning: TLS certificate verification is disabled (provide-io/pyvider:insecure-tls)\r\n\r\n  with provider[\"registry.opentofu.org/provide-io/pyvider\"],\r\n  on main.tf line 13, in provider \"pyvider\":\r\n  13:   api_insecure_skip_verify = true\r\n\r\nSkipping TLS certificate verification may be intentional for local development, but it permits man-in-the-middle\r\nattacks. Set api_insecure_skip_verify to false for safer connections. Suppress with !provide-io/pyvider:insecure-tls.\r\n"]
[12.609, "o", "\r\nWarning: Directory permissions are world-writable (provide-io/pyvider:world-writable-directory)\r\n\r\n  with pyvider_local_directory.lint_target,\r\n  on main.tf line 18, in resource \"pyvider_local_directory\" \"lint_target\":\r\n  18:   permissions = \"0o777\"\r\n\r\nWorld-writable permissions may be intentional for a shared scratch directory, but any local user can modify its\r\ncontents. Remove the POSIX other-write bit (for example, set permissions to 0o755) for a safer directory. Suppress with\r\n!provide-io/pyvider:world-writable-directory.\r\n"]
[12.609, "o", "\r\nWarning: HTTP API uses an unencrypted connection (provide-io/pyvider:insecure-http)\r\n\r\n  with data.pyvider_http_api.lint_target,\r\n  on main.tf line 23, in data \"pyvider_http_api\" \"lint_target\":\r\n  23:   url     = \"http://127.0.0.1/provider-lint-proof\"\r\n\r\nPlain HTTP may be intentional for a local endpoint, but request data can be intercepted or changed. Set url to an\r\nhttps:// address for a safer connection. Suppress with !provide-io/pyvider:insecure-http.\r\n"]
[12.609, "o", "\r\nWarning: Lease lifetime exceeds one hour (provide-io/pyvider:long-lived-lease)\r\n\r\n  with ephemeral.pyvider_lease.lint_target,\r\n  on main.tf line 32, in ephemeral \"pyvider_lease\" \"lint_target\":\r\n  32:   ttl_seconds = 3601\r\n\r\nA lease longer than one hour may be intentional for lengthy operations, but long-lived ephemeral values remain usable\r\nfor longer if exposed. Set ttl_seconds to 3600 or less for a safer lease. Suppress with\r\n!provide-io/pyvider:long-lived-lease.\r\n"]
[12.609, "o", "Success! The configuration is valid, but there were some validation warnings as shown above.\r\n"]
[16.299, "o", "OpenTofu core proof: 4/7 provider validation paths (provider, resource, data-source, ephemeral)\r\n"]
[16.299, "o", "\u001b[1;36m$ PYVIDER_LINT='provide-io/pyvider:all,!provide-io/pyvider:insecure-http' tofu validate\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[19.241, "o", "\r\nWarning: TLS certificate verification is disabled (provide-io/pyvider:insecure-tls)\r\n\r\n  with provider[\"registry.opentofu.org/provide-io/pyvider\"],\r\n  on main.tf line 13, in provider \"pyvider\":\r\n  13:   api_insecure_skip_verify = true\r\n\r\nSkipping TLS certificate verification may be intentional for local development, but it permits man-in-the-middle\r\nattacks. Set api_insecure_skip_verify to false for safer connections. Suppress with !provide-io/pyvider:insecure-tls.\r\n"]
[19.241, "o", "\r\nWarning: Directory permissions are world-writable (provide-io/pyvider:world-writable-directory)\r\n\r\n  with pyvider_local_directory.lint_target,\r\n  on main.tf line 18, in resource \"pyvider_local_directory\" \"lint_target\":\r\n  18:   permissions = \"0o777\"\r\n\r\nWorld-writable permissions may be intentional for a shared scratch directory, but any local user can modify its\r\ncontents. Remove the POSIX other-write bit (for example, set permissions to 0o755) for a safer directory. Suppress with\r\n!provide-io/pyvider:world-writable-directory.\r\n"]
[19.241, "o", "\r\nWarning: Lease lifetime exceeds one hour (provide-io/pyvider:long-lived-lease)\r\n\r\n  with ephemeral.pyvider_lease.lint_target,\r\n  on main.tf line 32, in ephemeral \"pyvider_lease\" \"lint_target\":\r\n  32:   ttl_seconds = 3601\r\n\r\nA lease longer than one hour may be intentional for lengthy operations, but long-lived ephemeral values remain usable\r\nfor longer if exposed. Set ttl_seconds to 3600 or less for a safer lease. Suppress with\r\n!provide-io/pyvider:long-lived-lease.\r\n"]
[19.241, "o", "Success! The configuration is valid, but there were some validation warnings as shown above.\r\n"]
